# The welcome card's close (x) button: the card with the x, its tooltip, and
# the map after a real click on the x. In script mode the dismissal is kept in
# memory only (the user's settings file is never written), and a saved
# dismissal never hides the card here, so this always starts with the card.
#
# The card is 560 wide, centred on the map area (window x 56..920, centre 488),
# so its right edge is x=768; the x button sits inside the 16px padding at the
# top right of the card.

window 1200 800
wait 3s
viewport 40.7128 -74.0060 16
wait_idle 5s
capture out/dismiss-1-card.png

hover 742,606
wait 2s
capture out/dismiss-2-tooltip.png

click 742,606
wait_idle 3s
capture out/dismiss-3-dismissed.png

# Even after removing a data layer the card stays away. (A script could also
# use `action DismissWelcome`.)
load_osm docs/screenshots/fixtures/select.osm
viewport 40.7120 -74.0060 18
wait_idle 5s
capture out/dismiss-4-data-loaded.png
